 R←Test_Create_004(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;res;stop;msg;rc;ref
⍝ Attempts to create a project with a namespace that is not fully qualified.
⍝ Such a name is taken as relative to the namespace Cider was called from, therefore Cider must ask
⍝ whether that namespace shall really be created. Here the question is answered with "No", so the
⍝ operation must be cancelled with nothing created at all.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 #.⎕EX'Goo'
 tempDir←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI

 ref←∆GetRefToCommTools
 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'CreateNamespaceWhileCreatingProject@' 'n'
 stop←0
 (rc msg res)←stop ∆UCMD'CreateProject "',tempDir,'" Goo -noEdit -ignoreUserExec'
 Assert 0=rc
 Assert 0=≢msg

 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'Cancelled by user'⍷res
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠#.⎕NC'Goo'                       ⍝ Neither in # ...
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠⎕THIS.⎕NC'Goo'                   ⍝ ... nor relative to the caller
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠≢⊃FilesAndDirs.Dir2 tempDir,'/'  ⍝ Not even a config file was written

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 ref.Cleanup
 rc←⊃FilesAndDirs.RmDir tempDir,'/..'
 Assert rc∧.=0
⍝Done
